# Patterns are matched against each path in the build context, and a pattern with no
# separator matches only at the top level - which is why the globs below are explicit.
# `**/` matches zero or more directories, so these cover the top level too.
# Measured sizes and the reasoning: docs/operations/docker.md#build-context

**/node_modules
.claude/
**/.git

# backend/Dockerfile is `COPY backend/ ./backend/`, so without these the production image
# shipped the test files plus cpython-314 bytecode into a python:3.12-slim image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
backend/test_*.py

# frontend/Dockerfile is `COPY frontend/public/ ...`, which published this on the production
# origin: GET /identify.test.js answered 200.
frontend/public/*.test.js

# test/, tools/, docs/, scripts/ and .github/ are deliberately NOT excluded. They are a few
# hundred KB next to the entries above, and a blanket exclusion is the kind of thing that
# makes a future `COPY test/ ...` copy nothing at all, with no error.

.certs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
